#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""ccfleet CLI: the original Claude Code interface, running on your slot.

The local process owns no Claude credential. It opens an authenticated WSS
byte path through the ccfleet broker, then OpenSSH provides end-to-end
encryption and host verification to the assigned slot. A forced remote entry
attaches to a persistent tmux session whose program is the original ``claude``.
The ``local`` command explicitly shares a selected project with that slot.
Claude and its tools still run on the slot; the laptop never runs a Claude agent
or an inference proxy. Returned file changes require review and conflict checks.
"""

